    "body": "## Description\nThis PR adds an explicit `IValue<string>` interface to `Base64Binary` through `JsonValue`.\n\n- The interface reads and writes Base64 text, not decoded file contents.\n- The interface returns the stored text. It does not decode this text into bytes.\n- If the value contains bytes, the interface encodes the bytes as Base64 text.\n- This PR does not change the public `Value` property or `IValue<byte[]>`.\n- This PR adds tests and a release note.\n\nThe second commit keeps the previous `IsNullOrEmpty()` behavior for `Base64Binary`.\nAn empty value is not a missing value.\nThus, snapshot generation keeps empty fixed, pattern, and default values.\n\n## Related issues\nFixes #3611.\n\n## Testing\nI did 77 selected tests on .NET 10. All 77 tests gave the correct results.\n\n```sh\ndotnet test src/Hl7.Fhir.Support.Poco.Tests/Hl7.Fhir.Support.Poco.Tests.csproj --no-restore --filter 'FullyQualifiedName~Base64Tests|FullyQualifiedName~ToSystemTypeTests|FullyQualifiedName~NullExtensionsTest|FullyQualifiedName~TestBase64Parsing'\n```\n\nThe new tests make sure that:\n- The interface gives the same Base64 string that the JSON or XML parser stored.\n- The decoded-byte cache stays empty before and after string access.\n- The interface converts bytes to Base64 text.\n- The two interfaces give the same value after a change through one interface or the other.\n- A missing value gives null.\n- An empty byte array is not a missing value.\n\nThe emptiness test failed before the correction and gave the correct result afterward. All 12 snapshot-generation cases kept the specified values.\n\nThe JSON/XML test uses `Ostrich` mode without model validation.\nDefault model validation can decode bytes when the parser loads a resource. This PR does not change that behavior.\n\nI did not do the full test suite, the package compatibility check, or the full CQL integration.\n\n## FirelyTeam Checklist\n- [ ] **Update the title** of the PR to be succinct and less than 50 characters\n- [ ] Mark the PR with the label **breaking change** when this PR introduces breaking changes\n",
